{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.CharacterDoubling","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.CharacterDoubling","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Trigonometric.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Log.Basic"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.CharacterDoubling.exists_q_dependent_residue_of_one_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.CharacterDoubling.exists_q_dependent_residue_of_one_le","kind":"theorem","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/CharacterDoubling.lean#L118-L123","doc":"So a `q`-dependent residue reproducing any requirement `≥ 1` exists by\nconstruction: the second survivor is vacuous, not open. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.CharacterDoubling.cosh_arcosh","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.CharacterDoubling.cosh_arcosh","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/CharacterDoubling.lean#L105-L116","doc":"`cosh` is onto `[1, ∞)`, witnessed explicitly. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.CharacterDoubling.not_constant_residue_character_of_doubling_fails","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.CharacterDoubling.not_constant_residue_character_of_doubling_fails","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/CharacterDoubling.lean#L79-L88","doc":"The contrapositive, quantified over all `c` at once: a function failing the\ndoubling identity at a single positive point is the character of no\nconstant-residue holonomy. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.CharacterDoubling.char_doubling_of_constant_residue","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.CharacterDoubling.char_doubling_of_constant_residue","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/CharacterDoubling.lean#L70-L77","doc":"Every constant-residue character satisfies the doubling identity, for every\n`c`. This is the hyperbolic analogue of `ln(q²) = 2 ln q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.CharacterDoubling.cosh_doubling","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.CharacterDoubling.cosh_doubling","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/CharacterDoubling.lean#L64-L68","doc":"The cosh double-angle law in the form the character test uses. ","signatureChunk":0}]}